phase P6
title Example apps
description
    **Class:** non-verifiable.

    **Goal:** medium-sized Next.js example apps in `examples/`, each importing the v3 package, each
    a striking demo that explains what it shows; one demos Story presentation. They also drive
    conformance runs and benchmarks.

    **Starts when:** P5's completion audit passes; the app pick may come any time before.

    **Verified by:** each decision's judge against the criteria; checkable parts: each app builds,
    lints, runs its Stories in `nub run verify`, and works in real Chrome and Safari.

    **One iteration:** one app's next slice, reviewed, then shown to the user.

    **Exit criteria:** every decision has its judge's ruling, and the user accepts each app.

    **False pass:** a demo that hides the guarantee it claims to show.

    **Caught by:** the user's review against the app's own write-up.

    **Gates:** each app's Stories in `nub run verify`, which reject one deliberately broken Story
    per app.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** picking the apps; accepting each app.

    **User's read:** each app's first working version; agent-judged slice calls.

    Decisions: which apps (judge: the user; candidates Pull the plug, Live auction, Agent console,
    Mission control, Smart home, Escape room, each with a live inspector panel showing `flow trace`
    and `flow graph`); each app's acceptance (the user, who set its requirements); design calls
    inside a slice (a reviewing agent, pending the user's read).

    Criteria (proposed, approved by the user before the first app):

    - each app explains what it demos with a write-up and in-place tooltips;
    - it shows one guarantee happening, not just a UI;
    - it runs in real Chrome and Safari;
    - one app demos Story presentation.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:interview for the pick and acceptance rounds;
    - skill:review per slice;
    - skill:check-runtime in real browsers.
tasks
    T32
        title       The user picks the apps and approves the criteria
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Put the candidate apps and the proposed criteria to the user in one numbered round; then add one Task per
            picked app with skill:to-task.

            **Why now:** P6 has no app Tasks until the user picks the apps and approves the criteria, and the pick may
            come
            any time before P6 starts.

            **Read first:** skill:interview, skill:to-task.

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): the criteria include a run
            in real Firefox (@plan.Package.O4), and the round decides whether Dispatch Desk and the seven entity
            examples (K10) are P6 apps or are cut from the Plan.

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Package.O4.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** criteria that a UI meets without showing a guarantee → caught by the
              criterion "shows one guarantee happening".
            - **Stops:** the pick itself.
        acceptance
            - The user's pick and approved criteria are recorded in an Epic note; one Task per app
            exists.
            - The Firefox criterion and the Dispatch Desk decision are recorded in the Epic note.
